    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170-a5">

                <pb facs="0357" n="229" xml:id="pg229"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. A. S. Lazarus &amp; Co. to Mr.
                    Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-10-26"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 26,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Noticing that the President of the United
                    States of Colombia has issued a proclamation declaring that on and after
                    December 1, 1885, import duties will be levied on imports into Aspinwall and
                    Panama, we ask the favor of a reply as to whether this is not in contravention
                    of treaties now existing between this country and that Republic.</p>
                <p>Soliciting the favor of an early reply, we have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>A. S. LAZARUS &amp; CO.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
